From d7393f3678a9c39b5c1e181922f29e13b727fddf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 16:27:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] nfc: add an NFC portal

There is no sanctioned way for a sandboxed application to use NFC. neard is a
system-bus service, so an application either gets the whole system bus or
nothing, and there is no per-app permission and nothing in Settings that says
which applications have asked.

This adds org.freedesktop.portal.NFC, modelled on the Camera portal: AccessNFC
prompts through the generic Access dialog and records the answer in the
permission store under table 'devices', id 'nfc'. Like Camera it needs no new
backend interface.

Deliberately no lockdown key. The camera has disable-camera because a camera
has no power switch; an NFC adapter has one, and the design makes
org.neard.Adapter Powered the single source of truth rather than adding a
second concept that could only disagree with it.

OpenNFCRemote is declared and refuses; the connection it hands out lands in the
next commit.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
